---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import CatStage from "../../components/CatStage.astro";
import DownloadCta from "../../components/DownloadCta.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema, softwareApplicationSchema } from "../../lib/site";

const path = "/blink-reminder/";
const title = "Blink Reminder App for Mac, Windows & Linux | Look Me";
const description = "A context-aware blink reminder that detects complete blinks locally, pauses when sensing is unavailable, and asks for two slow blinks after a long gap.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  schemas={[
    softwareApplicationSchema,
    breadcrumbSchema([{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Blink reminder", path }]),
  ]}
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath={path} />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">CONTEXT-AWARE BLINK REMINDER</p>
          <h1>Remember to blink <span class="soft-line">without watching another clock.</span></h1>
          <p>Look Me detects complete blinks on your device. After a prolonged gap, the desktop cat invites two slow blinks, then gives you space instead of repeating the prompt.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button" href="/download/">Download free</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy model</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">No target blink score. No camera upload. No medical diagnosis.</p>
        </div>
        <CatStage />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="sequence-heading">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN · CLOSE · OPEN</p><h2 id="sequence-heading">A complete sequence, not one noisy frame.</h2></div>
          <p>The detector combines both-eye blendshape signals with an eye-aspect-ratio check. It looks for a balanced transition and filters one-eye movement, long closure, and weak distant-face noise.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-rail">
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">01 / OBSERVE</span><h3>Confirm a usable face signal</h3><p>If confidence is low, the face is obscured, or camera access is unavailable, blink sensing pauses and the interface says why.</p></article>
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">02 / DETECT</span><h3>Recognize one full blink</h3><p>Both eyes need to move through a plausible open–closed–open sequence. A single uncertain frame is not enough.</p></article>
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">03 / RESPOND</span><h3>Mirror it with the companion</h3><p>The cat blinks back, making the invisible event visible without turning it into a score.</p></article>
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">04 / NUDGE</span><h3>Invite two slow blinks after a gap</h3><p>When the configured behavior detects a long no-blink interval, a small prompt appears. Completing two blinks ends it; a cooldown limits repetition.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="comparison-heading">
      <div class="shell-narrow article-body">
        <p class="eyebrow">TIMER VS SIGNAL</p>
        <h2 id="comparison-heading">Why not just set a repeating notification?</h2>
        <div class="comparison-table">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Behavior</th><th>Fixed timer</th><th>Look Me blink reminder</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>You step away</td><td>The clock continues.</td><td>Sensing pauses when no usable face signal is present.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>You already blink normally</td><td>The notification still arrives.</td><td>The no-blink interval restarts after a detected complete blink.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>The camera is blocked</td><td>The timer cannot know.</td><td>The app reports sensing as unavailable instead of fabricating a signal.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>You complete the prompt</td><td>You dismiss a notification.</td><td>Two detected blinks complete the interaction and begin a cooldown.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="article-callout">
          <strong>This is habit support, not dry-eye treatment</strong>
          <p>Look Me cannot diagnose dry eye disease, assess tear quality, or determine an ideal blink rate for you. Persistent or concerning eye symptoms require professional evaluation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <DownloadCta />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
